      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Red single crystals of CIAC-230 were obtained by solvothermal reaction of H8C8A (0.05 g, 0.04 mmol), Co(CH3COO)2·4H2O (0.04 g, 0.16 mmol), Dy(CH3COO)3·6H2O (0.05 g, 0.11 mmol), CH3OH/DEF (3 mL/3 mL), and triethylamine (0.1 mL) in a 20 mL Teflon-lined autoclave kept at 130 °C for 3 d, then slowly cooled to room temperature at about 4 °C h−1. Crystals were isolated by filtration, washed with methanol, and dried in air.",
